  "date": "11 October 2026",
  "summary_en": "The Pyro Activate node changes the activation of VDBs in a Pyro simulation. It turns voxel leaves on or off so the solver runs only where needed, while keeping enough surrounding air for the simulation.",
  "inputs": [
    "density: float VDB, the activation reference that also culls inactive leaves",
    "temperature: float VDB, used like density",
    "v: vector VDB supplying velocities for velocity dilation",
    "flame: float VDB, used like density",
    "activate_pts: points; any leaf containing a point is activated"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "References: fields that determine activation",
    "Density Cutoff: leaves whose maximum combined reference value falls below it can be deactivated",
    "Leaf Dilation / Leaf Dilation Dist: expand the active region by leaves or by world distance (rounded up to the leaf); the larger of the two is used",
    "Velocity Dilation: expands each leaf by its maximum velocity; related Velocity Scale, Tangential Scale and Ambient Velocity are not explained on the page",
    "Clip Min/Max X, Y, Z: deactivate leaves outside world-space bounds"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "COP Pyro requires DOP-level permissions; it is not in Houdini Core, only in FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education.",
    "Keep the simulated volume active with a buffer, or the surrounding air field may be missing.",
    "Leaves are 8x8x8 voxel blocks; fewer active leaves means less memory use and a faster simulation.",
    "The page covers the base node available since 21.0 and does not cover version 2.0."
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Pyro Activate active ou désactive les feuilles de voxels d'une simulation Pyro, pour ne résoudre que là où c'est nécessaire ; la page ne couvre pas la version 2.0."
